  sections={[
    { heading: 'Source records and attribution', paragraphs: ['Property records are imported from traceable public marketplace material and retain a source name, source URL where linking is allowed, and available source dates. This website does not describe those records as direct title filings, authenticated agent feeds, bank valuations or completed transaction reports.', 'A source reference helps a reader revisit the origin of a claim. It does not establish that the advertiser owns the property, can transfer it, has quoted a current demand or has described its condition accurately.'] },
    { heading: 'Normalization and quality controls', paragraphs: ['Import tooling converts source material into consistent fields for purpose, property type, location, size, price, images, status and dates. Quality checks identify missing required fields and likely duplicates. Local image validation makes sure each record points to an existing WebP file or the approved placeholder.', 'These controls improve website consistency, search and delivery. They do not replace document review, inspection, valuation or source reconfirmation.'] },
    { heading: 'Availability and freshness', paragraphs: ['Availability states determine whether a property appears in active results. A date-based freshness utility labels how recently the record was seen. These labels should be read as database state, not promises about live availability.', 'Third-party records can change between observations. Buyers should reconfirm the property ID, demand, source, seller authority and appointment immediately before acting.'] },
    { heading: 'Places and market information', paragraphs: ['Place pages organize directory records by category and sector, including addresses, public map links and recorded ratings where available. Business hours, services and locations can change, so contact the organization directly before travelling.', 'Market tables summarize the current asking dataset or present clearly labelled editorial indexes. They are not an official register of sale deeds, tax values or certified valuations. Comparable evidence should be checked for category, size, sector, street and date.'] },
    { heading: 'Corrections and official verification', paragraphs: ['Users may report stale availability, incorrect prices, classifications, place details or images through the contact channels. Include the record ID and supporting evidence so the underlying dataset can be reviewed.', 'Ownership, dues, NDC requirements, transfer eligibility, building approvals and official charges must be verified through DHA Lahore and suitable legal, tax, engineering or valuation professionals. Read the full property verification methodology for the boundary between portal checks and transaction due diligence.'] },
  ]}
  faqs={[
    { question: 'Does the website receive official DHA ownership data?', answer: 'No. The current dataset is not an official ownership register. Buyers must use DHA Lahore’s current process to verify property-specific records.' },
    { question: 'Are listed prices completed sale prices?', answer: 'No. They are advertised asking amounts unless explicitly and reliably identified otherwise.' },
    { question: 'How often is every property contacted?', answer: 'The website does not claim a guaranteed contact schedule for every third-party record. Use the displayed check date and reconfirm directly before acting.' },
    { question: 'How can an inaccurate record be corrected?', answer: 'Report the page and property ID through the contact channel with supporting information. The team can review the source and update the underlying record.' },
  ]}
